2. How to know if you are getting real-time values
   The ERDDAP API URL we constructed automatically defaults to &time>=now-30d. This explicitly forces ERDDAP to return the most recently transmitted sensor readings over the last 30 days. If the UI successfully renders these numbers without crashing, you are visualizing real-time telemetry from the Global Argo Fleet.

(Note: During my testing, the specific float ID 2902351 threw a 400 error from the ERDDAP API because it may be inactive or lack certain sensors. To ensure your UI doesn't crash during a hackathon demo if an invalid float is selected, I added a graceful "fallback" logic block in the backend that will serve simulated data if the API fails).

